            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Ezm9dXhbWoDyxuxcre6l6EMJg7f\">Regarding the remaining countries, Japanese teachers across all three levels had relatively similar teaching loads, ranging from 600 to 680 hours annually. Similarly, in Iceland, primary teachers spent approximately 600 hours teaching, though their secondary counterparts worked longer hours, at around 800 hours per year.</div>\n</div>",
